<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Long Australian bonds benefit from U.S..</title>
<headline>RTRS-Long Australian bonds benefit from U.S..</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> AUD VS   3-YR	   10-YR	* AUD 3-YR/10-YR SPREAD</p>
<p> USD	 55 (+ 06)   104 (UNCH) * FUTURES   84.5 (- 07.5)</p>
<p> CAD	173 (+ 13)    90 (+ 05) * CASH	89   (- 06)</p>
<p> NZD	-60 (- 02)   +03 (- 01) *</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Australian bond yield curve flattened as  the long-end benefitted from a strong U.S. market following Thursday's flow of market-friendly data and a positive response to a five-year note.</p>
<p>The local market was reasonably steady in spread terms against the U.S., but it was outperformed by the Canadian market which rebounded strongly after Wednesday's Canadian CPI-led sell-off.</p>
<p>-- Colin Brinsden - 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
